{"t": 162.836, "n": 121, "ev": "result", "ok": true, "text": "I wrote the plan to `docs/plans/i203a.plan.md`, status `planned`, complexity `complex`. I read the plan and documents rules and every spec the hand-off lists. I did not run any commands, as this step has no shell.\n\n**Complexity:** it has six phases, and the limit for `simple` is three. A `complex` plan carries phases, goals and weights only, so the expand step writes the task rows and the proof table.\n\n**Design**\n- A gate with no judge can't send a run back today. Phase 1 therefore adds `on_fail: back` to the engine (HUM-B15 to HUM-B18).\n- The unit is a script unit between `code` and `code_join`. Its script runs the due regenerations and commits. Its gate's check turns the results into findings, and the gate sends the run back to `code` once.\n- I took the defaults of the hand-off's open questions. The unit sits between `code` and `code_join`, an unusable declaration pauses, and there is no exception to the quick lane's file guard.\n\n**Phases**\n1. The engine's `on_fail: back`: validation and the trip back.\n2. The register rung for another checkout of a registered package (SCF-B24, SCF-B25).\n3. The declaration file, the unit, its blueprint entry and outcome criteria, and this repository's own declaration. This one is heavy (large-context).\n4. The numbered findings, the budget of one, the pause for a failure of the environment, and the code prompt.\n5. The phase and code gates, the reading list, and the plan, expand and code-judge briefs.\n6. The outcome revision, the README, the tests that pinned the old order of units, and CON-B7.\n\n**Requirements:** R1 to R12 cover AC 1 to AC 10. AC 9 is split across R9, R10 and R11.\n\n**Verification:** four commands. Three run in the engine folder (pytest, `ruff check src tests`, `mypy`). The fourth runs the package's own tests.\n\n**Docs to update**\n- `contracts.spec.md` (CON-B7)\n- the package `README.md`\n- `outcome.json`\n\n`stamp.json`, `authoring.json` and `diagram/` are generated files, so no row edits them by hand. The unit this run builds does not run in this run, so the code report will name those files for the operator. Criterion 10 allows that.\n\n**Extra files opened**, beyond the hand-off's list:\n- `test_workflow_packages.py`, for the command that runs a package's own tests.\n- A search for `on_fail` across the engine source and specs.\n- A search of `plugins/temperspec-tgraph/evals/`, for where calibration cases live.\n\nI read the plan and documents rule files, and also `spec.rule.md`, `task-notes.rule.md` and `extraction.rule.md`, which the session loaded as reminders.\n\nARTIFACT plan: docs/plans/i203a.plan.md\nARTIFACT complexity: complex", "subtype": "success", "is_error": false, "session_id": "7ded621d-ef4c-47e4-8dc8-9eed828a58c7"}
